00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.750 align:start position:0%
 
we're going to begin with this because  we've got an exclusive new interview  with brianna taylor's boyfriend his name  is kenneth walker  and he's telling cbs this morning he  cannot shake the trauma from the night  that she died  over the weekend protesters gathered in  taylor's hometown of louisville kentucky  and around the country demanding justice  over her death in a botched police raid  one year ago  walker was at that louisville rally and  was with taylor the night police raided  her home  the two were in bed at the time and  walker thought they were intruders  so he fired one shot from his weapon  that by the way he was legally  legally allowed to have and charges  against him were permanently dismissed  last week  we spoke with kenneth walker and his two  attorneys yesterday  every day feels like march the 14th to  me  every day does and i'm sitting right  here  today and i'm feeling tired tired  what are you tired of i'm tired of  having to get up every day and you know  and my life is it's changed i'm the only  person who has to deal with it every day  rihanna taylor's just a you know a  hashtag to other people but  she was something bigger than me of  course and it's hard to wake up every  day  and see you know her name and see her  pictures  and everything all over the place you  know but it's also like  that needs to happen because she still  hasn't gotten justice  yeah as we sit here today no one has  been charged  with her murder exactly  only one officer brett hankinson faces  charges for his actions at night  for wanton endangerment for shooting at  the apartment next door  last october two members of the grand  jury responsible for deciding charges  told us  they were never given the option of  charging the officers with murder  what did you think when you heard that  we were very surprised by that  only reason i wasn't surprised because  the way the whole situation has already  played out i'm still sitting here right  here as the only person who's been to  jail  and i didn't kill anybody what's that  man get me on your knees  walker was arrested and charged with  assault and attempted murder  accused of shooting sergeant jonathan  mattingly during the raid  walker's legal team says ballistic's  evidence does not prove his bullet  struck mattingly  last week a judge dismissed those  charges permanently  you were sort of in limbo kenneth  because they could have charged you at  any time without the charges being  dropped  so when you got the news that they had  been dropped did you feel relieved  when i heard the news i was definitely  relieved but also it's kind of like a  smack in the face too  because there should have never been any  charges in the first place  what does that say to you about the  initial charges since they've now  dismissed it  his wary of the police showing up at his  house any night and  charging him with uh you know attempted  murder again  is over but there has to be  accountability  to what happened not only to brianna but  what happened to kenny  because they clearly just charged kenny  in an attempted cover-up for brianna's  killing  and then that house of cards basically  just fell apart  easily and the charges against kenny are  dismissed and they just want to walk  away  and we've said repeatedly no it is not  okay to just walk away  there has to be a consequence because  without a consequence there's  never accountability i've heard people  say that you don't move on but you move  forward  there's several steps i'm taking as far  as the healing process but i mean of  course i talked to a therapist good  on the regular kenneth last time we  talked to you you weren't sure you were  going to do that  but my mind you know it's not right you  know every  nothing's right so you know  got to try new things in new situations  so with all the love and support that  brianna's receiving and i'm receiving  there's also a lot of hate too  you are receiving hate are you the most  famous one that i've seen is that people  said that i used brianna as a human  shield  oh my god that's that's been said on the  internet but like i said i mean if you  were to do  any type of research or look into  anything that's not even possible  but kenneth let's stop on that for just  a second what a cruel thing to say to  you  most definitely but these are things  that i have to deal with on the daily  so far well for me to be getting sued  you know for something like emotional  distress when i have to deal with things  like that every day  that's another slap in the face let's  talk about that because it raised a lot  of eyebrows when officer mattingly  the officer who was hit in the leg that  night  filed a counter suit against you  claiming alleged battery assault and  emotional distress  you heard that lawsuit and you thought  what i thought that's everything that  happened to me  but you know okay the truth always  wins so have you been able to go back to  work yet  no i've definitely not been able to go  back to work and  you know that's that's another thing  that i miss out on but even if i was  to be able to go to work right now it  wouldn't be normal when he's applying  for jobs people are asking you ever been  arrested  so the the reality of that situation is  he  has suffered both psychological and  economic damage as a result of what's  happened  right and someone's going to have to  rectify that and it's the parties that  we have sued we believe  last week walker filed a federal lawsuit  against the louisville city government  police department and officers involved  in the raid  he alleges they violated his fourth  amendment right to be free  from unreasonable searches what do you  miss most about  brianna everything  but i'd say on the daily like the help  that she gave me like even just  just simple things like remembering you  know what what day my phone bills do  stuff like that like i wouldn't have to  worry about that  well isn't it kenneth the simple things  isn't it  the everyday things you know that i'm  missing out on  are are we hurt the most  jefferson county commonwealth's attorney  tom wine told cbs news his office  dropped the charges against kenneth  walker  because it determined it did not have  sufficient evidence to prove his guilt  at trial  we also by the way reached out to the  kentucky attorney general that's daniel  cameron's office  the louisville metro police department  and sergeant mattingly's attorney  all parties declined to comment and  that's what struck me  at the end of the interview it's the  it's the simple things  being involved in a couple don't forget  to pay your phone you can i could bring  something because as soon as he said  that i could like i could  i know you know you always think about  the big things in life but it's the  small things i mean his life has been  permanently permanently changed as we  see and i thought his attorney fred  moore raised a good point when he said  when you fill out an application it says  have you been arrested that's something  that says that makes a big difference  but you know it's the little things but  i think about the big things too they  were  baby clothes i mean yeah yeah no telling  where they would be right now if not for  this intervention and in that lawsuit  they said listen it's not about money  but  certainly money gets people's attention  to lead to change and he's certainly  owed something for what he has been  through  so we'll be following these cases  certainly more to come

